   "text": "I read the structure in sections and wrote each piece as SMILES. I took the stereocentres from the wedges and hashes as drawn, checking the proline and tert-leucine centres against the standard VHL-ligand configuration.\n\n- **Left end:** a 3-cyano-pyrrolo[1,2-b]pyridazine joined at its pyrrole carbon (C7) to a pyridine. The pyridine carries an NHMe group at the 4-position and the thiadiazole at the 5-position.\n- **Core linker:** a 1,3,4-thiadiazole links to a trans-1,4-disubstituted cyclohexane, drawn with one wedge and one hash. The cyclohexane nitrogen is acylated as a succinamide, \u2013NHC(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)NH\u2013.\n- **tert-Leucine:** the succinamide continues into a tert-leucine unit with a tert-butyl group.\n- **Hydroxyproline:** the tert-leucine carbonyl joins the nitrogen of a 4-hydroxyproline. Its (2S,4R) configuration matches the wedges drawn.\n- **Right end:** the proline carboxamide is linked through a benzylamine to a para-substituted phenyl bearing a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\nFor the cyclohexane I worked out the chirality tags so the two substituents come out trans.\n\nSMILES: N#Cc1cnn2c(c1)ccc2-c1cc(NC)c(cn1)-c1nnc(s1)[C@H]2CC[C@@H](CC2)NC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)NCc1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
